{"title":"2023 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the following arrangement of positive integers.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>The 1st row includes the odd integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the 2nd row includes the two even integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84c0da6f9bb05c6b3f2db89eea12691e4b79066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />th row\n</p>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: circle\">\n<li>begins with the integer that is one more than the last integer in the previous row,</li>\n<li>begins with the integer that is one more than the last integer in the previous row,</li>\n<li>includes, in increasing order, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive odd integers when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is odd, and</li>\n<li>includes, in increasing order, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive even integers when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is even.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A useful fact about this arrangement is that the integer in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />th row and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />th position (that is, the last position in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />th row) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00ff2fd800eb5e3300360954f5880cd34273bee3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" />. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0e9136809f832318fdd66a5180d0e20660e072b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^{2} = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" /> and 16 is the integer in the 4th position of the 4th row.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which row has the integer 145 in the 1st position?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For the first number in the row to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/0/7d00d6cfbf7dab73af54367e971ffc25a4091499.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$145$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, the last number in the previous row must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50ff9540650f0f95f80da2f6692fc8ee413e2eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> because\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of the previous row. Since the integer in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />th row and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />th position is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00ff2fd800eb5e3300360954f5880cd34273bee3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c212c385d0fe27663f6cc7c512a75c5ae176809a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^{2} = 144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/870abbafb82181d468f7188bf6c6599bceea4edf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\sqrt{144} = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the row with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/0/7d00d6cfbf7dab73af54367e971ffc25a4091499.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$145$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> in the first position is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/c/9ec51fe74986dcb633a5439c9f6fa40012761564.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + 1 = 12 + 1 = \\boxed{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"171\" height=\"25\" />th row.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018023517\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.029 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 89/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1994/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4187/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   16.700      1 2023_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%   16.700      1 -total\n 33.97%    5.673      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35536:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018023517 and revision id 277861. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}